WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.360
You all know how much I love scary mazes and
theme parks, so I just have to talk about

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.700
this trailer for Hellfest.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:10.010
This is gonna be a pretty short video though,
so just roll the intro.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:16.020
OK, as soon as I saw this scene with the hammer,
I was thinking it would be really cool if

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.160
that was used as a weapon somewhere in the
movie.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.000
And sure enough at the end of the trailer
here, there's a quick shot of the stalker

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.000
using it as a weapon.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.880
I also thought that the slider being a zombie
head thing was a nice touch and this could

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:29.890
be a metaphor for the point that we're reaching
maximum intensity in this movie.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:32.910
The friend character has all of this hippie
stuff in her room, so I wonder if there's

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:36.410
going to be a scene where she has a chance
to take out the killer or something, and she

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:37.800
doesn't because she's all anti-violent.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.980
I don't know, just a thought.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.469
I was looking at some of the themed areas,
because I love analysing that stuff in theme

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:44.469
parks.

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:54.290
I mean, I used to do theme park videos when
I was a kid.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:55.930
So there were two areas that stood out to
me.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.420
The first being this, which maybe like an
evil twist on Alice in Wonderland, with these

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:03.329
Mushrooms and the decaying trees back here,
and then this like a guy standing in a big

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.129
zombie head teacup thing.

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:08.090
The announcer is a kind of like a mad hatter
type of character.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:11.719
Then the other area I thought was interesting
was maybe like a haunted school theme, which

00:01:11.719 --> 00:01:13.420
I think is actually pretty unique idea.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.310
You've got a classroom, a gym locker room,
and a hallway.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.719
I like seeing some original themed areas that
aren't just intellectual property based, but

00:01:19.719 --> 00:01:23.270
it looks like this movie will feature some
characters who are kind like parodie horror

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.270
IPs.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:29.189
We've got knockoffs of Saw, The Strangers,
Beetlejuice, Predator, The Walking Dead...

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:32.969
and some that are probably not intentional
but I'm gonna mention anyways just for laughs

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:36.909
like Argghus, The Earthshapers and... wait
a minute this one actually looks strikingly

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:37.909
similar.

00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:39.520
One of the lines in this trailer gave me an
idea.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:40.520
Roll that clip.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.869
"The same guy's been following me the entire
night."

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:47.889
I actually like the idea of a theme park hiring
a few character actors to just stalk certain

00:01:47.889 --> 00:01:48.979
groups the entire night.

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:53.770
Like if I owned a horror nights type thing,
I'd have maybe 5-10 actors that I tell to

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:55.750
just shadow the same group of kids.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:58.460
It would be way creepier than any of the mazes.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:01.670
I know that's not what's going on in Hell
Fest, but I just thought I'd share that idea,

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:02.799
I think it's pretty cool.

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:05.920
Like I said, not a whole lot to talk about
here, so if you're looking for more content

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.330
this week, I was in a collab where I play
this creepy camp counselor, so go check this

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.330
video out.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:15.030
Al Dente Creepypasta is coming back with a
new episode next week, so make sure you're

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:19.920
subscribed to CZsWorld for new horrors every
week, ring that deathbell for notifications

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.260
and I'll see you in the next one.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.319
Assuming we both survive.

